# 2 Baruch Chapter 48 — The LOGOS Bible (Formal)
**Translator:** LOGOS | **Source:** Syriac MS (Codex Ambrosianus 7a1) | **Section:** Fourth Fast and Dialogue

---

**1** And it came to pass after these things that I prayed and said: "O Lord, you who called into being that which did not exist, who brings down that which has not yet come, and who reveals what is hidden —

**2** you who sustain life by your power, and have decreed death by your will, and made known pain by your counsel;

**3** you who measured the firmament by a span and the dust of the earth in a vessel, and weighed the mountains in a balance and the hills in a scale,

**4** you who stretched out the heavens as a veil and established the earth upon the waters;

**5** you who made the springs of fire emerge and the dark waters beneath the heavens, and set the springs of the deep in their places,

**6** you who enclosed the sea by your word and restrained the deep by your power, and dried up the great waters of the primordial deep by your wisdom,

**7** you who created man by your word and ordered all the generations of humanity by your wisdom;

**8** you to whom the depths of the abyss and the dark chambers of the earth are revealed, and to whom the dwelling places of the dead are subject;

**9** you who know before they come what the coming years will bring, and what the passing years contain;

**10** you whose kingdom endures forever, and whose glory no end can describe;

**11** you before whose greatness the hosts of angels tremble, and whose glory all the works of fire serve;

**12** you whose decrees the fire and the hail obey, and whose commands the snow and the frost fulfill;

**13** you who set apart a people for yourself from all the nations, which is called your firstborn, your only-begotten, and your beloved;

**14** you who made a covenant with our father Abraham, and swore to Isaac, and established it with Jacob;

**15** you who brought your people out of the land of Egypt, out of the furnace of iron, and led them through the way of the desert,

**16** you who fed them with manna and gave them water from the rock, and kept them under the shadow of the cloud by day,

**17** you who gave them your law and set righteousness before them, and established for them the covenant of life;

**18** you who gave them commandments and statutes and set before them the way of life and the way of death;

**19** hear, O Lord, my prayer now! For you have not hidden yourself from the groaning of your people.

**20** "For you know what we have done, and our fathers transgressed before you, and now you have punished us according to our ways.

**21** Do not remember the deeds of our fathers against us, but be mindful of your power and your name at this time.

**22** For we have sinned and transgressed your statutes, and you are the righteous one, O Lord our God.

**23** But do not destroy us as the nations who have never known you; do not deal with us as those peoples who have never called upon your name.

**24** For there is none among the nations that has not sinned before you, and they all lack understanding; but among us, your people, there is knowledge, though it may not be perfect.

**25** "I know that you are angry, yet you have not destroyed us utterly, for we are those upon whom you have bestowed your mercy.

**26** Did you not divide the world between Adam and his posterity? And did you not make known to them the ways of your understanding?

**27** Did you not place in them the seed of eternal life, and show them the paths of correction?

**28** And you gave them the beginning of wisdom and the understanding of truth;

**29** and you promised them life and threatened them with death; and at the end of times you will judge them.

**30** "But now, turn your mercy toward us, for we are those who have called upon your name;

**31** and though we have sinned, yet we have received your discipline; and those who scattered us will not endure forever.

**32** Consider those among the nations who do not know you, who live as though there is no judgment;

**33** for you know all the secrets of the world and everything hidden beneath the earth, and all the thoughts of men.

**34** You know the end of time and the day when all will be revealed before you;

**35** and you know the number of births and the number of deaths that have not yet come;

**36** you know how many will perish in fire and how many in waters, and how many will be preserved by the sword and how many in captivity;

**37** you know how many will be consumed by beasts and how many by worms, and how many will receive death by pestilence;

**38** and you know whether the end of the ages will come through great power or through quiet rest.

**39** "O Lord my God, you alone know the depth of your wisdom and the breadth of your understanding, and no one can fathom the counsel of your mind.

**40** Truly, the heaven itself is too small to contain you, and how much more then these buildings constructed by men!

**41** But you have chosen this people and called this land holy, and you have taken up your dwelling here for your name.

**42** And now you have allowed the nations to trample upon it, and those who hate us have prevailed over us.

**43** Our enemies have laughed at us, and those who hated us have rejoiced in our downfall.

**44** What will become of your name, O Lord? What will be said of your glory among the nations?

**45** Are you not the one who promised that Zion would be restored? And are you not the one who said that your people would be gathered together?

**46** Yet now we are scattered, and our enemies have prevailed, and there is none who helps us.

**47** "Do not forget your servants, O Lord, for we did not depart from your law by our own will, but were taken captive against our will.

**48** And though we were scattered among the nations, yet we kept your law in the midst of our affliction.

**49** And now, O Lord, look upon us and be gracious to us, for you alone are our hope, and apart from you there is no salvation for us.

**50** For if you do not have mercy on us, there is none who will save us; and if you do not gather us, we will perish."

---

*LOGOS notes: Formal equivalence rendering from the Syriac (Codex Ambrosianus 7a1). Paragraph divisions follow the sense units of the source.*
